====Usage notes====
* The genitive plural ''ēsa'' (attested in ''ēsa gescot'' “the shot of the ''ēse''”) and names such as ''Esegar'' display i-mutation, despite being a u-stem. This is likely a fossilization from an earlier stage between {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*ansu}} and early Old English {{m|ang|*ons}}, in which i-mutation was applied to the attested declined forms due to the word’s archaic meaning, rather than its active usage.
