=====Usage notes=====
* Becomes -{{m|pt|los}} after verb forms ending in ''-r, -s'', or ''-z'', the pronouns {{m|pt|nos}} and {{m|pt|vos}}, and the adverb {{m|pt|eis}}; the ending letter causing the change disappears.
*: After {{m|pt|ver}}: {{ux|pt|Posso vê-los?|May I see them?|inline=1}}
*: After {{m|pt|por|pôs}}: {{ux|pt|Pô-los ali.|He put them there.|inline=1}}
*: After {{m|pt|fazer|fiz}}: {{ux|pt|Fi-los ficarem contentes.|I made them become happy.|inline=1}}
*: After {{m|pt|nos}}: {{ux|pt|Deu-no-los relutantemente.|He gave them to us reluctantly.|inline=1}}
*: After {{m|pt|eis}}: {{ux|pt|Ei-los!|Behold them!|inline=1}}
* Becomes -{{m|pt|nos}} after a nasal diphthong: ''-ão, -am'' {{IPAchar|[ɐ̃w̃]}}, ''-õe'' {{IPAchar|[õj̃]}}, ''-em, -êm'' {{IPAchar|[ẽj̃]}}.
*: {{ux|pt|Detêm-nos como prisioneiros.|They detain them as prisoners.|inline=1}}
* In Brazil it is being abandoned in favor of the nominative form {{m|pt|eles}}.
*: {{ux|pt|Eu os vi. → Eu vi eles.|I saw them.|inline=1}}

